ATTRIBUTION

This Rust implementation is a faithful port of the original C program,
maintaining compatibility with the original's configuration files, command-line
interface, and behavior. The modular structure in Rust mirrors the functional
organization of the original cping.c.

Module Mapping:
- main.rs      → Main event loop and initialization
- ping.rs      → Ping/Stat structures and ByteTime encoding
- icmp.rs      → ICMP packet handling and checksums
- dnscache.rs  → DNS resolution and caching
- config.rs    → Configuration file parser and options
- app.rs       → Application state management
- net.rs       → Network sockets and send/receive threads
- ui.rs        → TUI rendering (replaces ncurses with ratatui)
- output.rs    → Log file writing
- gpio.rs      → Raspberry Pi GPIO support (optional)

All credit for the original design, algorithms, and functionality goes to
Willem A. Schreuder. https://www.prinmath.com/ham/cping.zip
